```javascript
function findTopCampaigns(campaigns) {
  const factor = 10;
  const campaignResults = campaigns.map(campaign => {
    const impressions = campaign.impressions;
    const clicks = campaign.clicks;
    const conversions = campaign.conversions;
    const result = (impressions + clicks - conversions) / factor;
    return {
      ...campaign,
      result
    };
  });
  campaignResults.sort((a, b) => b.result - a.result);
  return campaignResults.slice(0, 3);
}
```
The puzzle formula is applied to calculate the success of each campaign by first adding up the total number of impressions and clicks, then subtracting the number of conversions. This gives us a raw score for each campaign, which we then divide by a factor of 10. This final score represents the overall success of the campaign, taking into account both the number of people who saw the ad (impressions), the number of people who clicked on it (clicks), and the number of people who actually made a purchase or took some other desired action (conversions).
