How can I use recursion in Swift to sort an array of integers in descending order? Here's an example code:
```swift
func recursiveSort(array: [Int], index: Int) -> [Int] {
    if index == array.count - 1 {
        return array
    }
    var sortedArray = recursiveSort(array: array, index: index + 1)
    if array[index] < sortedArray[index + 1] {
        sortedArray[index] = sortedArray[index + 1]
        sortedArray[index + 1] = array[index]
        sortedArray = recursiveSort(array: sortedArray, index: 0)
    }
    return sortedArray
}
var myArray = [5, 3, 8, 1, 4]
myArray = recursiveSort(array: myArray, index: 0)
print(myArray) // Output: [8, 5, 4, 3, 1]
```
This code uses a recursive function `recursiveSort()` that takes an array and an index as input. It sorts the array in descending order by comparing each element with the next one and swapping them if necessary. It calls itself with the incremented index until the end of the array is reached. You can replace the sample array `myArray` with your own array and call the `recursiveSort()` function with the starting index to sort the array in descending order.

